Fix GICD active-bit semantics.

The distributor handlers for GICD_ISACTIVER and GICD_ICACTIVER kept the
old "not implemented" placeholder: a write to ISACTIVER cleared the bit
instead of setting it, so the vGIC could never report an SPI active.  The
firmware self-test's dist.active probe writes ISACTIVER and reads it back,
which would fail on the first hardware boot even though the image ships
that probe.

Make both registers write-1-to-set / write-1-to-clear over the same
bitmap, mirror the aliases, and drop the placeholder errors.

diff --git a/src/hv_vgic.c b/src/hv_vgic.c
--- a/src/hv_vgic.c
